  "paragraph": 7,
  "text": "That gives us a crisp division of labor. The model owns reasoning, judgment, and planning, the messy probabilistic work where large language models shine. Surrounding that core, the harness owns everything deterministic: executing tools reliably, keeping context hygiene tight, enforcing hard safety perimeters, and delivering ground-truth feedback from the real world. Whenever you feel tempted to solve a reliability bug by stuffing more rules into a prompt, stop and ask whether the harness should own that guarantee in code instead.",
